# Code owners for canon.
#
# Every pull request automatically requests review from the owner matched
# here. The LAST matching pattern wins, so the catch-all sits at the top and
# more specific areas override it below.
#
# Enforcement: CODEOWNERS only *requests* review by default. To make owner
# review a merge requirement, enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the
# branch protection rule for `main` (Settings → Branches).
#
# These all resolve to the same person today — GOVERNANCE.md is honest about
# that, and this project's own canon records it as data (`canon who canon`).
# When a second person holds standing over a scope, splitting an area off is
# a one-line change here and a `canon grant` in `.canon/acts.jsonl`. Which
# of those two is the real event is the open question in `canon open`.

# Default owner for everything.
*                               @alexsbryan

# --- The compatibility promise ---------------------------------------------
# The record format is CC0 and other implementations read it. A change here
# is a promise to them, not just to this repository. `adequacy_bar` gates a
# new op mechanically; what it cannot judge is whether the op should exist.
/SPEC.md                        @alexsbryan
/crates/canon-core/src/act.rs   @alexsbryan

# --- The fold --------------------------------------------------------------
# Pure by construction: no filesystem, no network, no model. The way to break
# that is to add a dependency, so the manifest gets owner eyes too.
/crates/canon-core/             @alexsbryan
/crates/canon-core/Cargo.toml   @alexsbryan
/Cargo.toml                     @alexsbryan
/rust-toolchain.toml            @alexsbryan

# --- The tool --------------------------------------------------------------
/crates/canon-cli/              @alexsbryan

# --- Evidence --------------------------------------------------------------
# Fixtures are open to outside pull requests and review is mostly mechanical
# — a worked canon replays or it does not. The part that is NOT mechanical is
# provenance: where the source came from and whether it may be vendored at
# all. That judgement is why this is still owned.
/fixtures/                      @alexsbryan

# The pre-registered bars. A bar edited after seeing the data it tests is not
# a bar, so a diff here is read against the run that motivated it.
/crates/canon-cli/tests/        @alexsbryan

# --- Machinery -------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/                       @alexsbryan
/.githooks/                     @alexsbryan
/scripts/                       @alexsbryan

# --- Governance ------------------------------------------------------------
# This project's own rules. A diff here is a governance act: the log is
# append-only, so a change that is not a new line at the end is a rewrite of
# the record and should be rejected on sight.
/.canon/                        @alexsbryan
/GOVERNANCE.md                  @alexsbryan
/CLA.md                         @alexsbryan
/LICENSE                        @alexsbryan
